        "original_id": "f49a32bf-aaa9-54c8-a894-67932d6a2be3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jonny Craig, Pete Doherty, Carl Barât\n- Bands and Projects: Dance Gavin Dance, Emarosa, Ghost Runner on Third, Slaves, westerHALTS, the Libertines, Babyshambles, Peter Doherty and the Puta Madres\n- Albums and Songs: The Greatest of All Lost Arts, \"Pueblo Cicada\"\n\nFacts:\n- Pete Doherty formed the Libertines with Carl Barât in 1997.\n- Jonny Craig was born on March 26, 1986, and he is a Canadian-American singer and songwriter.\n- Jonny Craig has been the lead vocalist for Dance Gavin Dance, Emarosa, Ghost Runner on Third, Slaves, and westerHALTS.\n- Pete Doherty is best known as the co-frontman of the Libertines.\n- Pete Doherty's other musical projects include Babyshambles and Peter Doherty and the Puta Madres.\n- The album The Greatest of All Lost Arts contains 11 tracks.\n- Jonny Craig provided guest vocals on the song \"Pueblo Cicada\" from The Greatest of All Lost Arts.",
